 "verdict_note": "Corrected for the $3.2bn regulatory fee (both legs), the cost of financing the long and a break value centred on the factor model ($613): about +5.3% a year above Treasuries on margin capital at 48% completion odds, just over the 5% hurdle (it needs a 21.0% spread). The edge rests on LITE being worth about $613 on its own; with the first version's blended break value ($512) it is -3.2% a year, and the stress case loses. One lot per $10k at most."
